      "title": "Australian politics live: Hastie ‘lived a lot’ of SAS report findings; Paterson accuses PM of ‘no standards’ over golf club",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/29/labor-treasurer-jim-chalmers-social-media-anthony-albanese-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Gas reservation policy set for lower house vote today</strong></p><p>Australia’s domestic gas reservation is set to be debated and voted on in the lower house today.</p><p><em>Rather than international base companies, determining through algorithms what Australians receive, it empowers people themselves to determine what you receive on your devices, so that you should have that control.</em></p><p><em>This isn’t about government having a greater role. It’s about people having a greater role, having more control themselves, and it’s deserving of support of this parliament.</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/29/labor-treasurer-jim-chalmers-social-media-anthony-albanese-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T03:05:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australian SAS officers knew about unlawful ‘throwdowns’ on dead Afghans, report says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/29/australian-sas-officers-knew-about-unlawful-throwdowns-on-dead-afghans-report-says-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Nothing done to stop planting weapons on dead Afghans, ADF inspector says, as ‘breakdown of command’ allowed ‘egregious behaviour’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Some Australian SAS officers knew that soldiers under their command were using “throwdowns” – planting weapons on dead Afghan civilians to portray them as combatants – but did nothing to stop the unlawful practice, a previously unpublished military report has said.</p><p>Posted online this week, the <a href=\"https://www.igadf.gov.au/system/files/2026-10/Executive%20Summary%20of%20the%20IGADF%20Inquiry%20into%20the%20Cultural%20Context%20in%20which%20Command%20over%20SOTGs%20or%20Special%20Forces%20Personnel%20was%20exercised%20in%20Afghanistan.pdf\">executive summary of a 2021 investigation</a> into the “cultural context” of the special operations command by the inspector general of the Australian Defence Force (IGADF) is scathing about the “breakdown of command” and the erosion of military discipline during special forces operations in Afghanistan, which “resulted in episodes of potential and actual egregious behaviour”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/29/australian-sas-officers-knew-about-unlawful-throwdowns-on-dead-afghans-report-says-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T00:30:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Worldwide legacy’: almost $20m raised to protect majestic tract of land in far north Queensland",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/29/worldwide-legacy-almost-20m-raised-to-protect-majestic-tract-of-land-in-far-north-queensland",
      "description": "<p>Bush Heritage hopes to buy Wooroora station, which links wet sclerophyll forest and savanna woodland and is home to 12 endangered species  </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A majestic tract of land in far north Queensland that links wet tropics and world heritage rainforest, and contains headwaters that flow to the Great Barrier Reef, could be bought and protected by Christmas, after a conservation group raised more than $19m in private donations to buy the cattle station.</p><p>Wooroora spans more than 20,000 hectares of largely intact wet sclerophyll forest and savanna woodland on the lands of the Jirrbal people about 100km south-west of Cairns – and borders Bush Heritage’s existing 43,575-hectare Yourka Reserve in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/apr/22/conservationists-rubbish-plan-to-build-a-windfarm-near-protected-north-queensland-rainforests\">one of the most biodiverse regions in Australia</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/29/worldwide-legacy-almost-20m-raised-to-protect-majestic-tract-of-land-in-far-north-queensland\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T21:06:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Don’t be stinky’: recruitment a ‘huge issue’ facing Aukus submarine program",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/australia-must-recruit-hundreds-more-to-crew-aukus-submarines-retired-admiral-warns",
      "description": "<p>As USS Colorado showcases the program in Perth, retired admiral Peter Briggs says personnel is one of the ‘huge issues’ it faces</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/29/labor-treasurer-jim-chalmers-social-media-anthony-albanese-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia faces an uphill battle to recruit and train enough naval personnel to serve on submarines planned for the future fleet of nuclear-powered vessels under <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/18/paul-keating-aukus-locking-australia-into-us-china-war\">the controversial $368bn Aukus deal</a>, a retired admiral has warned.</p><p>As the Virginia-class submarine USS Colorado arrived at HMAS Stirling south of Perth on Tuesday for a month of routine maintenance and to help build Australian expertise, retired admiral Peter Briggs said more people needed to be enrolled in the navy’s submarine program.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/australia-must-recruit-hundreds-more-to-crew-aukus-submarines-retired-admiral-warns\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T12:46:36"
    }
  ]
